Z||000023||terryk||08-06-99||12:20 AM||||If you can swap a 3.8L in, you can handle the associated ECM swap. Chips are available to disable VATS and the 92/3 ECM will support the 125C/440 trans.<p>I swapped a 3.8L SC with the 4T60E into my 86 Ciera GT. The wiring was most of the work.<p>However, on my 86 2M6 Fiero, I am looking to turbocharging. For all of the fabrication work to Vaseline a V8 in there or the exhaust work needed for the 3.8L (they output on the back, not the front, a good turbo, pipe work and a Syclone 1227749 ECM is easier and will produce about as much power. Sure, my SC is more torquey, but the swap with a manual trans is not easy. The flywheel must be custom. The N car 3.0L manual trans flywheel might work though.<p>The Fiero can run on the 1227749 ECM with some code changes. The ECM can be found in Quad 4's, Sunbird Turbo's, and of course Syclones and Typhoons (like they will let you have it!) Use the Sunbird or SyTy mem-cal as a starting point.
